solution.p:
Let h be the height of the person in Zoeys model, which well measure in inches. Well create a proportional equation that compares the building and persons heights in the model to their heights in real life:
\begin{aligned}
\frac{\text{height of model building in inches}}{\text{height of actual building in feet}}\amp=\frac{\text{height of model person in inches}}{\text{height of actual person in feet}}\\
\frac{3\,\text{in}}{64\,\text{ft}}\amp=\frac{h\,\text{in}}{5\,\text{ft}\,6\text{in}}
\end{aligned}
Before we can just eliminate the units, well need to convert 5 ft6 in to feet:
\frac{2\,\text{in}}{30\,\text{ft}}=\frac{h\,\text{in}}{5.5\,\text{ft}}
Now we can remove the units and continue solving:
\begin{aligned}
\frac{3}{64}\amp=\frac{h}{5.5}\\
\multiplyleft{64\cdot5.5}\frac{3}{64}\amp=\frac{h}{5.5}\multiplyright{64\cdot5.5}\\
5.5\cdot 3 \amp= 64h\\
16.5 \amp= 64h\\
h\amp\approx 0.2578125
\end{aligned}
Zoey should make the model be {0.257812\ {\rm in}} tall.
